# Public keys allowed to sign my commits, so `git log --show-signature` and
# %G? can verify them instead of reporting "No principal matched".
#
# Keys are from github.com/stefanvanburen.keys; principals are the committer
# emails each key has signed under. namespaces="git" keeps them usable for
# commits and tags only, not for SSH auth or arbitrary `ssh-keygen -Y`.
#
# Principals are labels, not a constraint: git verifies by looking the key up in
# this file and reports whichever principal it is listed under, so it checks
# "one of my keys signed this", not "this identity signed this". Commits made
# under a work identity verify from these entries too -- no extra principals,
# and no work addresses in a public repo.

